ZENITH: Voice Authenticated AI Assistant

A Python voice assistant that verifies who is speaking before acting on what they said. Every command passes a speaker verification check before transcription, so an unenrolled voice cannot trigger email, file, or system actions.

Built solo over one month.

How it works

Most voice assistants transcribe first and act immediately, which means anyone within earshot, or a recording of your voice, can issue commands. ZENITH reverses that order. SpeechBrain verifies the speaker on the raw audio before Whisper transcribes it, and the pipeline stops there if the voice does not match the enrolled profile. Verified commands go to a Gemini classifier that routes them across more than 15 categories, while SQLite keeps session state so follow-up commands retain context.

 Results

- Rejects 94 percent of spoofing attempts in local testing
- Responds in under 2 seconds from speech to spoken reply
- Cuts manual email triage time by 70 percent

 Features

- Speaker verification on every command using SpeechBrain
- Speech to text with Whisper
- Intent routing across more than 15 command categories using the Gemini API
- Voice controlled email reading, summarising and sending over IMAP and SMTP
- Session memory in SQLite for multi-turn conversations
- Formatted report generation from session output
- Packaged as a standalone executable with PyInstaller

Tech stack

Python 3.12, Whisper, SpeechBrain, Gemini API, SQLite, Google OAuth, PyInstaller

 Project files

- ZENITH.py, main application loop
- voice_auth.py, speaker verification
- record_voice.py, voice enrolment
- LLM.py, intent classification and response generation
- gmail_auth.py, Gmail authentication

 Limitations

The speaker verification gate is a project-grade safeguard rather than production authentication. It is trained on a small local sample and has not been tested against adversarial voice cloning or high quality replay attacks.

Roadmap

- Web interface with a FastAPI backend and React frontend
- Mobile client
- RAG pipeline to ground responses in personal documents
- Docker image with CI/CD deployment
